.SH NAME
ivcap-artifact-upload - Resume uploading artifact content


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBivcap artifact upload artifactID -f file|- [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Resume uploading content to an existing artifact.

.PP
Local ZIP, TAR and TAR.GZ archives are indexed before upload and receive an RO-Crate 1.2 JSON-LD
manifest aspect by default. Use --without-manifest to opt out. Content read from stdin cannot be
indexed and is uploaded without a manifest.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chunk-size\fP=10000000
	Chunk size for splitting large files

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--content-type\fP=""
	Content type of artifact; auto-detected when omitted. Accepts a full MIME type (e.g. application/x-compressed-tar) or a bare extension (e.g. tgz, nc, fasta)

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	Path to file containing artifact content

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for upload

.PP
\fB--manifest-schema\fP="urn:ivcap:schema:artifact.archive-manifest.1"
	Schema URN for the archive manifest aspect

.PP
\fB--without-manifest\fP[=false]
	Do not add a file manifest for ZIP, TAR or TAR.GZ archives


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--access-token\fP=""
	Access token to use for authentication with API server [IVCAP_ACCESS_TOKEN]

.PP
\fB--context\fP=""
	Context (deployment) to use

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Set logging level to DEBUG

.PP
\fB--no-history\fP[=false]
	Do not store history

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	Set format for displaying output [json, yaml]

.PP
\fB--silent\fP[=false]
	Do not show any progress information

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30
	Max. number of seconds to wait for completion


